        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "consolidateAccountEngagement"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 5689,
            "y": 7742
          },
          "code": "CONSOLIDATEACCOUNTENGAGEMENT",
          "id": "1775205501565",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775205501599_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "INPUT DATA:\n {{$context.$nodes.LOOPENGAGEMENTS.$output}} \n \nGOAL:\nConsolidate all account-level engagement summaries (emails, calls, activities) into a single unified \"direct_account_engagement\" structure without losing any information.\n\nINSTRUCTIONS:\n- The input contains multiple objects from different engagement channels, each following the same engagement schema.\n- Merge ALL inputs into ONE final \"direct_account_engagement\" object.\n\nMERGING RULES:\n\n1. OVERALL SUMMARY:\n- Generate a single consolidated \"summary\" across ALL engagement types (emails, calls, activities).\n- Reflect overall account engagement behavior, activity level, and interaction trends.\n- Highlight cross-channel patterns such as:\n  - Increased or decreased engagement\n  - Consistency or gaps across channels\n  - Shifts in communication or activity intensity\n\n2. SENTIMENT:\n- Combine sentiment insights from all sources.\n- Identify dominant sentiment (positive / neutral / negative).\n- Reflect overall account tone across communications and interactions.\n- Provide one concise summary.\n\n3. PRODUCT FOCUS, INDUSTRY FOCUS, SIGNALS:\nEach must contain:\n- \"summary\" → high-level synthesis across ALL sources\n- \"details\" → MUST include ALL unique factual points from emails, calls, and activities\n\nDETAILS RULES (CRITICAL):\n- Do NOT drop any information from any source.\n- Merge and deduplicate overlapping points.\n- Preserve specific facts such as:\n  - Product names, features, and use cases\n  - Industry references and context\n  - Engagement signals (interest, objections, follow-ups, commitments)\n  - Actions, meetings, discussions, and outcomes\n- Ensure coverage across ALL channels (emails + calls + activities).\n\n4. CROSS-SOURCE CONSOLIDATION:\n- Treat all inputs as complementary signals of the same account.\n- Merge insights across channels intelligently:\n  - If the same signal appears in multiple sources → consolidate (do not repeat)\n  - If different signals appear across sources → include ALL\n- Do NOT bias toward any single channel.\n\n5. NO DATA LOSS:\n- Every important fact from every input must appear in the final output (especially in \"details\").\n\n6. NO DUPLICATION:\n- Avoid repeating identical or semantically similar statements.\n- Merge overlapping insights cleanly.\n\n7. ACCOUNT-LEVEL CONSOLIDATION GUIDELINES:\n- Focus on:\n  - Overall engagement intensity across the account\n  - Breadth of interactions (emails, calls, activities)\n  - Decision-making signals and buying intent (if present)\n  - Consistency or fragmentation across contacts/channels\n- Do NOT reduce to individual contact behavior unless necessary for context.\n\n8. STRUCTURE:\n- Output ONLY ONE object.\n- Maintain EXACT schema as defined below.\n\n9. STRICT OUTPUT:\n- Output must be valid JSON only.\n- No explanations, no extra text.\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT:\n{\n  \"summary\": \"string\",\n  \"sentiment\": {\n    \"summary\": \"string\"\n  },\n  \"product_focus\": {\n    \"summary\": \"string\",\n    \"details\": \"string\"\n  },\n  \"industry_focus\": {\n    \"summary\": \"string\",\n    \"details\": \"string\"\n  },\n  \"signals\": {\n    \"summary\": \"string\",\n    \"details\": \"string\"\n  }\n}\n\nSTRICT OUTPUT RULES (CRITICAL):\n\n- Output MUST be raw JSON object.\n- DO NOT wrap output in ```json or any markdown.\n- DO NOT return as string.\n- DO NOT escape quotes.\n- DO NOT add backticks.\n- DO NOT add newline escape characters (\\n).\n- Response must start with { and end with } only.\n- If a field has no supporting data, output exactly \"\". Do not generate filler, assumptions, risk statements, status labels, or placeholder phrases of any kind.\n- All keys defined in the output schema are mandatory and must be included even when no data is available; in such cases, use \"\" as the value.\n  Example fallback output when no data exists:\n  {\n  \"summary\": \"\",\n  \"sentiment\": {\n  \"summary\": \"\"\n  },\n  \"product_focus\": {\n  \"summary\": \"\",\n  \"details\": \"\"\n  },\n  \"industry_focus\": {\n  \"summary\": \"\",\n  \"details\": \"\"\n  },\n  \"signals\": {\n  \"summary\": \"\",\n  \"details\": \"\"\n  }\n  }\n"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
